---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

import { LAST_UPDATED, formatLastUpdated } from '@/lib/page-dates.mjs';

const lastUpdated = formatLastUpdated(LAST_UPDATED.refunds);

// DRAFT. Sentences marked data-review="jurisdiction" depend on the law of
// the customer's country or the contracting entity; data-review="processor"
// marks a claim about the payment processor's behaviour to confirm against
// its current docs. All need a maintainer's review, and counsel's before
// the first charge. The markers render nothing; grep for data-review to list
// them.
---

<Layout
  title="Refund and Cancellation Policy - Legesher"
  description="How cancellation, refunds, failed payments and plan changes work for paid Legesher subscriptions."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-32 pb-20 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-4xl">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-2">Refund and Cancellation Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Legesher Inc (Delaware, USA) ·
          <span>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
        </p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:text-foreground prose-a:text-brand-cyan hover:prose-a:text-brand-coral prose-table:text-sm">
        <section aria-labelledby="introduction">
          <h2 id="introduction">1. Introduction</h2>
          <p>
            This policy explains what happens when you cancel a paid Legesher subscription, when you can get a refund,
            and what happens if a payment fails. It applies to every paid plan sold through our checkout. It forms part of
            our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>; the Terms control if the two conflict.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nothing in this policy affects the Legesher open-source software, which is free under the Apache 2.0
            License and is not a subscription. You never need a paid plan to write code in your language with the
            open-source tools.
          </p>
          <p>
            <span data-review="jurisdiction">If you are a consumer, you may have rights under the law of your country
            that this policy cannot reduce. Where that law gives you more than this policy does, the law applies.</span>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="who-bills-you">
          <h2 id="who-bills-you">2. Who Bills You</h2>
          <p>
            Paid Legesher subscriptions are sold through <a href="https://polar.sh" rel="noopener">Polar</a>, which acts
            as the merchant of record. <span data-review="jurisdiction">Polar is the seller on your receipt, collects
            payment and any applicable sales tax or VAT, and issues refunds; Legesher Inc decides the plan, the price
            and this policy.</span> Polar's own terms apply to the payment itself.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your subscription, invoices, payment method and cancellation are all managed from the Polar customer
            portal. The link to the portal is in every receipt email and in your Legesher account.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="cancellation">
          <h2 id="cancellation">3. Cancelling a Subscription</h2>
          <p>
            You can cancel at any time from the Polar customer portal. You do not need to email or call us.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Access continues to the end of the period you paid for.</strong> Cancelling stops the next renewal;
              it does not end the current period early. Your plan's features keep working until the paid period ends,
              then your account moves to the Free plan.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>You can undo a cancellation</strong> from the portal at any time before the period ends, and the
              subscription continues as if nothing happened.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Nothing you built is removed.</strong> Code and translations in your own repositories stay
              there. When the paid period ends, the hosted service stops translating new changes. Hosted copies of
              your data are kept until you ask us to delete them (see Section 7).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Founding Developer (beta) seats.</strong> A founding seat is tied to an active subscription. If you
              cancel, the seat is released at the end of the paid period; if you later subscribe again, you join on the
              plan and price in force at that time.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="refunds">
          <h2 id="refunds">4. Refunds</h2>

          <h3>4.1 New subscriptions</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-review="jurisdiction">If a paid plan is not what you expected, ask for a refund within
            <strong>14 days</strong> of your first payment and we will refund that payment in full.</span> After that window, the first period is not refundable, but you can cancel at any time (Section 3).
          </p>
          <p>
            <span data-review="jurisdiction">The 14-day window is our policy and applies worldwide. If the consumer law
            where you live gives you a longer withdrawal period for digital services, that period applies instead.</span>
          </p>

          <h3>4.2 Renewals</h3>
          <p>
            <span data-review="jurisdiction">A monthly renewal charged in error, or charged after you tried to cancel and
            the cancellation did not take effect, is refunded in full if you contact us within 14 days of the
            charge.</span> Otherwise renewals are not refunded; cancel before the renewal date to avoid the next charge.
          </p>

          <h3>4.3 Annual plans</h3>
          <p>
            Annual billing is not offered yet. If it is introduced, this section will state the proration rule before the
            first annual plan is sold.
          </p>

          <h3>4.4 Enterprise agreements</h3>
          <p>
            Enterprise customers are billed by invoice under a signed agreement. Refunds and termination for those
            agreements follow the agreement, not this policy.
          </p>

          <h3>4.5 How refunds are paid</h3>
          <p>
            Refunds go back to the original payment method through Polar. <span data-review="processor">Once
            approved, a refund usually appears within 5 to 10 business days, depending on your bank or card
            issuer.</span> A refund ends access to the paid plan at the moment it is issued.
          </p>

          <h3>4.6 What is not refunded</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Usage already consumed, such as hosted imports that have run, except inside the windows above</li>
            <li>Charges for a period in which the account was suspended for a breach of the Terms</li>
            <li>Currency conversion fees or bank charges applied by your own bank</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="failed-payments">
          <h2 id="failed-payments">5. Failed Payments</h2>
          <p>
            If a renewal payment fails, we tell you by email and Polar retries the card. During the retry period your
            account runs with Free plan limits and nothing is removed.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Grace period.</strong> <span data-review="jurisdiction">You have 17 days from the first failed
              charge to update your payment method in the Polar portal.</span> As soon as a payment succeeds, your paid
              plan is restored.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>After the grace period.</strong> The subscription is cancelled and the account stays on the Free
              plan. You can subscribe again at any time.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Account data.</strong> Hosted account data from a cancelled subscription is kept for
              <span data-review="jurisdiction">60 days</span> so you can come back without starting over, then removed
              under our data retention rules. Data in your own repositories is never touched.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="plan-changes">
          <h2 id="plan-changes">6. Upgrades, Downgrades and Price Changes</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Upgrades</strong> take effect immediately. <span data-review="processor">Polar charges the
              prorated difference for the rest of the current period.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Downgrades</strong> take effect at the end of the current period. You keep what you paid for until
              then; no partial refund is issued for the difference.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Price changes.</strong> We do not raise the price of a plan you already pay for without at least
              90 days' notice by email, and you can keep your current price for the remainder of any period already
              paid. The price you were quoted at checkout is the price you pay for that period.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="data-after-cancellation">
          <h2 id="data-after-cancellation">7. Your Data After Cancellation</h2>
          <p>
            Cancelling a subscription is not the same as deleting your account. Hosted copies of your maps and account
            data are kept after your subscription ends, until you ask us to delete them, so you can return without
            starting over.
            To delete your account and its hosted data, email
            <a href="mailto:privacy@legesher.com">privacy@legesher.com</a>; how we handle that request is described in
            our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="how-to-ask">
          <h2 id="how-to-ask">8. How to Ask for a Refund</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>Email <a href="mailto:hello@legesher.com">hello@legesher.com</a> from the address on your account.</li>
            <li>Include the receipt number from Polar (it is on the receipt email) and the reason, if you want to share one.</li>
            <li>
              We reply within <span data-review="jurisdiction">3 business days</span>. Approved refunds are issued through
              Polar straight away.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            Disagreements about a refund are handled under the dispute section of our
            <a href="/terms#governing-law">Terms of Service</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="changes">
          <h2 id="changes">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy. The date at the top changes when we do, and for material changes we email
            subscribers before the change takes effect. A change never reduces the refund rights of a period you
            have already paid for.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="contact">
          <h2 id="contact">10. Contact</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Plans, payments and refunds: <a href="mailto:hello@legesher.com">hello@legesher.com</a></li>
            <li>Account help: <a href="mailto:support@legesher.com">support@legesher.com</a></li>
            <li>Legal notices: <a href="mailto:legal@legesher.com">legal@legesher.com</a></li>
            <li>Privacy and account deletion: <a href="mailto:privacy@legesher.com">privacy@legesher.com</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-12">
          <em>Effective date: {lastUpdated}</em>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Keep heading anchors clear of the fixed header on in-page navigation */
  :global(main h2[id]),
  :global(main h3[id]) {
    scroll-margin-top: 6rem;
  }
</style>
